 slot but lists no specific dates, so confirm the next date. A separate \u017Di\u017Ekostel series ran editions in March and May 2026 at 450 to 750 K\u010D, but no later dates were found."}),y("Taiz\xE9 prayer, Church of St Martin in the Wall","spirit",["2026-12-07","2027-01-04","2027-02-01","2027-03-01"].filter(h=>Qe(+h.slice(0,4),+h.slice(5,7))===h),"First Monday of the month \xB7 19:30",g(19,30),"Church of St Martin in the Wall, Martinsk\xE1 8, Prague 1",[A],{ll:[50.0830247,14.4198306],free:0,pr:"Price not listed",note:"Held on the first Monday of each month except July and August. The page lists dates only up to June 2026, so these dates follow its rule. Singing in several languages, readings in English and Czech."}),y("Sunday services, Church of St Martin in the Wall","spirit",st("2026-11-15",Ze,[6]),"Weekly, Sundays \xB7 10:30 in German, 19:30 in Czech",g(10,30),"Church of St Martin in the Wall, Martinsk\xE1 8, Prague 1",[Z],{ll:[50.0830247,14.4198306],pr:"Price not listed"}),y("Sunday Eucharist, St Clement's Anglican church (English)","spirit",st("2026-11-15",Ze,[6]),"Weekly, Sundays \xB7 11:15",g(11,15),"St Clement's, Klimentsk\xE1 5, Prague 1",[fe],{ll:[50.09202,14.4291],free:0,pr:"Price not listed",note:"The page gives 11:15, while its welcome text says 11:00. Evensong is held on the first and third Wednesdays of the month (time not listed)."}),y("Evensong, St Clement's Anglican church (English)","spirit",[_e(2026,12,1),_e(2026,12,3),_e(2027,1,1),_e(2027,1,3),_e(2027,2,1),_e(2027,2,3),_e(2027,3,1),_e(2027,3,3)],"First and third Wednesday of the month \xB7 time not listed",null,"St Clement's, Klimentsk\xE1 5, Prague 1",[fe],{ll:[50.09202,14.4291],pr:"Price not listed",note:"Based on the 1662 Book of Common Prayer. The page gives the pattern, not exact dates, so these follow its rule. Time not listed."}),y("Sunday programme at the Hare Krishna temple, Lu\u017Ece","spirit",st("2026-11-15",Ze,[6]),"Weekly, Sundays \xB7 from 14:00",g(14),"Hare Krishna temple, Lu\u017Ece 48 (outside Prague)",[ee],{free:0,pr:"Price not listed",note:"The Sunday programme starts with arati, then chanting, a lecture on the Bhagavad-gita and a feast. The temple is in Lu\u017Ece, outside Prague, not in the city."}),y("Govinda vegetarian restaurant (Hare Krishna centre)","spirit",st("2026-11-15",Ze,[0,1,2,3,4,5]),"Mon\u2013Fri 11:00\u201318:00, Sat 12:00\u201316:00",[660,1080],"Soukenick\xE1 27, Prague 1",[me],{og:1,ll:[50.0912,14.4337],pr:"Price not listed",note:"Vegetarian restaurant founded in 1995, with a sweet shop. It is listed as an ISKCON centre. Sunday opening is not listed. Cash and meal coupons only, no cards."}),y("Christmas Eve family masses","spirit","2026-12-24","Thu 24 Dec \xB7 around 16:00",g(16),"Various churches in Prague",[ke],{free:1,pr:"Free entry",note:"The page does not name the churches or the language."}),y("Christmas Eve mass, T\xFDn Church","spirit","2026-12-24","Thu 24 Dec \xB7 16:30",g(16,30),"T\xFDn Church, Old Town Square",[ke],{free:1,ll:[50.0877,14.4213],pr:"Free entry",note:"Free, just turn up. The page does not give the language."}),y("Open-air Christmas mass, Old Town Square","spirit","2026-12-24","Thu 24 Dec \xB7 21:00",g(21),"Old Town Square stage",[ke],{free:1,ll:[50.0875,14.4213],pr:"Free entry"}),y("Midnight Mass, Strahov Monastery Basilica and other churches","spirit","2026-12-24","Thu 24 Dec \xB7 24:00",null,"Strahov Monastery Basilica and several other churches",[ke],{free:1,ll:[50.0861,14.3883],pr:"Free entry",note:"The page says service times are often announced close to the date. Language not stated."}),y("Night of Churches","spirit","2027-06-04","Fri 4 Jun 2027",null,"Churches across Prague",[Ge],{pr:"Price not listed",note:"Listed as an open day with no time, price or venue list."}));const j={"Guided meditation, Diamond Way Buddhist Centre (English)":"A weekly guided meditation at a Buddhist centre of the Diamond Way (Karma Kagyu) tradition. This Thursday session is the English one.","Guided meditation, Diamond Way Buddhist Centre (Czech)":"The centre's regular guided meditations on the 16th Karmapa on the other days of the week, held in Czech. Monday starts with an introduction to the centre.","The Life of Marpa (talk), Diamond Way Buddhist Centre":"An evening on the life of Marpa, the Tibetan translator and teacher in the Kagyu lineage.","Prague meditation weekend, Diamond Way Buddhist Centre":"A weekend of meditation at the Diamond Way Buddhist centre.","Ecstatic Dance Project Prague (weekly)":"Free-form, no-talking dance session to a DJ set, usually barefoot and alcohol-free. No dance experience needed.","Sound healing bath and deep relaxation, Studio AnYo":"A relaxation session where you lie in a hammock while singing bowls, chimes and other instruments play, with guided meditation. Suitable for beginners.","Taiz\xE9 prayer, Church of St Martin in the Wall":"A quiet evening of prayer with repeated chants and silence in the style of the Taiz\xE9 community. Open to everyone.","Sunday services, Church of St Martin in the Wall":"Evangelical Sunday services in a historic Old Town church: German in the morning and Czech in the evening.","Sunday Eucharist, St Clement's Anglican church (English)":"English-language Anglican Sunday service in central Prague, with children's ministry on most Sundays.","Evensong, St Clement's Anglican church (English)":"A sung evening service in English, based on the 1662 Book of Common Prayer.","Sunday programme at the Hare Krishna temple, Lu\u017Ece":"The weekly Sunday gathering of the Hare Krishna community: temple ceremony, chanting, a talk on the Bhagavad-gita and a vegetarian feast.","Govinda vegetarian restaurant (Hare Krishna centre)":"Long-running vegetarian restaurant and sweet shop run in the Hare Krishna tradition, in central Prague.","Christmas Eve family masses":"Short Christmas Eve masses for families with children, held in several Prague churches.","Christmas Eve mass, T\xFDn Church":"Christmas Eve mass in the T\xFDn Church, the Gothic church overlooking Old Town Square.","Open-air Christmas mass, Old Town Square":"A Christmas Eve mass held outdoors on Old Town Square, next to the Christmas tree and markets.","Midnight Mass, Strahov Monastery Basilica and other churches":"The traditional Christmas midnight mass, held at several Prague churches including the Strahov Monastery Basilica.","Night of Churches":"An annual open night when churches and religious buildings across Prague open to visitors, often with music and tours."};u.forEach(h=>{j[h.n]&&(h.d=j[h.n])}),i.art="Art & workshops";const we=["Open Art Fest, PVA EXPO","https://www.pvaexpo.cz/en/event/517"],Ce=["Kunsthalle Praha: November programme","https://www.kunsthallepraha.org/en/articles/november-in-kunsthalle-praha-discover-our-program"],Ye=["Fine Art Studio: workshop listings","https://www.malovanikresleni.cz/en/sluzby/"],Ue=["Prague Life Drawing Workshop","https://praguelifedrawingworkshop.carrd.co/"],se="Fine Art Studio, Balb\xEDnova 28, Prague 2",He="Workshop dates and prices as listed on the studio's page. Booking is through the studio.";u.push(y("Open Art Fest 2026","art",["2026-11-28","2026-11-29"],"28\u201329 Nov \xB7 9:00\u201318:00",[540,1080],"PVA EXPO Praha, Hall 1, Beranov\xFDch 667, Prague 9",[we],{lo:250,hi:250,pr:"Admission 250 K\u010D, children under 15 free",ll:[50.1385,14.516],note:"Painting workshops for adults and children on both days, a live art battle on Saturday 16:00\u201318:00 (12 painters, secret theme), free children's theatre at 11:00 and 15:00, and a photography workshop on Saturday 14:00\u201316:00. Advance tickets through Ticketmaster.",d:"A two-day art fair where about 360 artists show and sell original paintings, sculpture, photography and design, so you can meet the artists. The organiser calls it the largest gathering of visual artists in Central Europe."}),y("Guided tour: Tragikomedie, Witchcraft and Magic, Kunsthalle Praha","art","2026-11-29","Sun 29 Nov \xB7 16:00",g(16),"Kunsthalle Praha (address not on the page)",[Ce],{ll:[50.09232,14.40963],note:"In Czech, according to the page.",d:"A guided tour of the Tragikomedie exhibition, with a focus on witchcraft and magic."}),y("Art 101: Why Is This Art? (talks), Kunsthalle Praha","art",["2027-01-18"],"18 Jan \u2013 15 Feb 2027 \xB7 times not listed",null,"Kunsthalle Praha (address not on the page)",[Ce],{ll:[50.09232,14.40963],og:1,r:["2027-01-18","2027-02-15"],note:"English-friendly according to the page. The page gives the series dates but no times.",d:"A short series of talks that asks what makes something art."}),y("Life drawing session (uninstructed), Prague Life Drawing Workshop","art",st("2026-11-16","2027-03-31",[0]),"Weekly, Mondays \xB7 18:00\u201320:00",[1080,1200],"Venue not stated for this session on the page",[Ue],{pr:"Price not listed",note:"The page lists a weekly Monday 18:00\u201320:00 uninstructed session but does not name the venue or price for it.",d:"Draw from a live model with no teacher. Bring your own materials."}),y("Dry pastel workshop, Fine Art Studio","art",["2026-11-21","2027-01-30"],"Sat 21 Nov and Sat 30 Jan \xB7 time not listed",null,se,[Ye],{ll:[50.077,14.434],lo:1500,hi:1500,pr:"1 500 K\u010D",note:He}),y("Japanese calligraphy workshop, Fine Art Studio","art",["2026-11-22","2027-01-10"],"Sun 22 Nov and Sun 10 Jan \xB7 time not listed",null,se,[Ye],{ll:[50.077,14.434],lo:2e3,hi:2e3,pr:"2 000 K\u010D",note:He}),y("Christmas workshops, Fine Art Studio","art","2026-11-28","Sat 28 Nov \xB7 time not listed",null,se,[Ye],{ll:[50.077,14.434],lo:1300,hi:1300,pr:"1 300 K\u010D",note:He}),y("Impressionist painting for children aged 8+, Fine Art Studio","art","2026-12-05","Sat 5 Dec \xB7 time not listed",null,se,[Ye],{ll:[50.077,14.434],lo:1300,hi:1300,pr:"1 300 K\u010D",note:He}),y("Mosaic workshop, Fine Art Studio","art","2026-12-06","Sun 6 Dec \xB7 time not listed",null,se,[Ye],{ll:[50.077,14.434],lo:2500,hi:2500,pr:"2 500 K\u010D",note:He}));const Ae={x122:"A studio workshop on shading and working with light in drawing, building the tonal skills behind realistic form.",x123:"A hands-on dry pastel workshop at a Vinohrady-area fine art studio. Materials are usually provided, no experience needed.",x124:"An introduction to Japanese calligraphy: brush handling, stroke order and the basic characters, in a small studio class.",x125:"Seasonal creative workshops at the studio, making Christmas decorations and gifts by hand.",x126:"A relaxed painting class for children aged 8 and up, exploring the colour and light of Impressionism.",x127:"A hands-on mosaic workshop: cut, arrange and fix small pieces into a decorative piece to take home.","mk-miru":"A neighbourhood Christmas market on N\xE1m\u011Bst\xED M\xEDru in Vinohrady, with the Church of St. Ludmila as a backdrop. Mulled wine, seasonal food and handmade gifts.","mk-rep":"Christmas market by the Municipal House and Powder Tower on Republic Square. Food stalls, drinks and seasonal gifts, a bit calmer than the Old Town.","mk-tylak":"A small local Christmas market on Tylovo n\xE1m\u011Bst\xED in Prague 2, with festive stalls and refreshments.","mk-main":"Prague's best-known Christmas markets, around the big tree on Old Town Square and along Wenceslas Square. Trdeln\xEDk, sausages, mulled wine, crafts and a stage programme.","mk-hol":"A Christmas edition of the Hole\u0161ovice Market hall area, mixing food, drink and seasonal stalls away from the tourist centre.","mk-and":"A Christmas market in the And\u011Bl pedestrian zone in Sm\xEDchov, with seasonal stalls and refreshments.","mk-kul":"The Advent edition of a Saturday neighbourhood market, with local food, produce and seasonal goods.","mk-mint":"A design and handmade market held in a hall at the Hole\u0161ovice Market: independent makers, vintage, food and drink.","mk-karl":"A one-day Christmas gathering in Karl\xEDn with a tree lighting, stalls and festive drinks.","mk-lesser":"A small market on Malostransk\xE9 n\xE1m\u011Bst\xED in Lesser Town, with stalls on selected evenings.","mk-nap":"The riverside farmers' market on N\xE1plavka: local produce, baked goods, street food and coffee, with views of the Vltava.","mu-korn":"Californian nu-metal band on tour, heavy riffs and a big arena show.","mu-prod":"British electronic and breakbeat act known for high-energy, loud live shows.","mu-sb":"A winter-themed show by the English soprano, mixing classical-crossover and pop repertoire.","mu-4s":"Vivaldi's famous violin concertos, played in the grand Art Nouveau Smetana Hall.","mu-boc":"A programme of popular classical favourites performed in the Municipal House.","mu-ave":"A candlelit classical concert of Ave Maria settings in a historic Old Town church.","mu-moz":"Dinner with live piano music at a historic caf\xE9 on Old Town Square.","mu-xc":"Christmas-season classical concerts in two historic Prague venues.","mu-stm":"Early-evening Christmas concerts in the Klementinum, a short classical programme in a historic setting.","st-nab":`Verdi's opera about the Babylonian king Nabucco, famous for the chorus "Va, pensiero". Performed at the Prague State Opera.`,"st-trav":"Verdi's tragic love story of Violetta, a Parisian courtesan. One of the most performed operas in the world.","st-flute":"Mozart's fairy-tale opera of Prince Tamino and Pamina, with the Queen of the Night. Staged at the Estates Theatre, where Mozart conducted.","st-don":"Mozart's dark comedy about the seducer Don Giovanni, premiered in Prague in 1787 at the Estates Theatre.","st-onegin":"A ballet based on Pushkin's tale of love, pride and regret, performed at the National Theatre.","st-swan":"Tchaikovsky's classic ballet of Odette, the swan princess, and the prince who loves her.","st-nut":"Tchaikovsky's Christmas ballet about a girl, a toy nutcracker and a journey to the Land of Sweets.","ex-press":"The yearly exhibition of award-winning Czech press photography, covering news, sport, nature and daily life.","ex-hp":"An immersive exhibition with sets, props and costumes from the Harry Potter film world.","ex-blanka":"An exhibition at the Municipal House dedicated to the work of the artist Blanka Matragi.","ex-banksy":"An exhibition of works and projects connected to the street artist Banksy, held in a historic church.","ex-ng":"A day of free admission to the permanent collections of the National Gallery venues listed.","ex-lich":"An open day at the Liechtenstein Palace on Kampa Island, normally closed to the public.","ex-beth":"A Christmas exhibition in the crypt of Bethlehem Chapel, the Old Town church linked to Jan Hus.","ex-antique":"A fair of antiques, collectibles and vintage objects at the New Town Hall.","sk-letna":"An outdoor ice rink in Letn\xE1 Park with views over the city. Skate hire is available.","sk-vyst":"An indoor ice rink at the V\xFDstavi\u0161t\u011B exhibition grounds, so it works in any weather.","sk-fran":"An ice rink in the centre of Prague, a short walk from Old Town.","sk-wenc":"A pop-up winter ice rink on Wenceslas Square, in the middle of the Christmas atmosphere.","sk-ovoc":"A small ice rink beside the Estates Theatre, close to the Old Town markets.","fe-wine":"A festival celebrating the first wine of the year, held in the vineyards below Prague Castle.","fe-krampus":"A show based on the Czech Mikul\xE1\u0161 tradition of the saint, the angel and the devil.","fe-film":"A festival of recent French cinema screened in Prague cinemas.","fe-castle":"A day of Christmas programme at Prague Castle, with the seasonal decorations and events.","fe-castle2":"Christmas events and markets in the grounds of Prague Castle.","fe-vine":"Christmas-themed events at the St. Wenceslas Vineyard, with views over the city.","fe-cruise":"A sightseeing cruise on the Vltava with an Advent theme, passing Prague's riverside landmarks.","fe-lamp":"A lamplighter in period costume lights the lamps on Charles Bridge, a short Advent tradition.","fe-nye":"How Prague celebrates New Year's Eve: crowds on Old Town Square and Wenceslas Square, plus river and viewpoint spots."},tt={Edis:"Bulgarian pop-folk star Edis live in Prague.","Prague Sounds: Paul Hillier and Theatre of Voices":"A vocal-music performance by the Theatre of Voices, part of the Prague Sounds festival.","Jos\xE9 Gonz\xE1lez":"The Swedish-Argentine singer-songwriter, known for gentle acoustic guitar songs.","Prague Sounds: Steve Reich 90":"A concert marking the composer Steve Reich's 90th birthday, part of Prague Sounds.","Little BIG":"Russian rave-pop band Little BIG, known for their wild, funny videos.","Prague Sounds: Samara Joy":"The American jazz singer Samara Joy performs at the Rudolfinum, part of Prague Sounds.","Martina P\xE1rtlov\xE1":"Czech singer and songwriter Martina P\xE1rtlov\xE1 in a big arena show.","Portugal. The Man":'American indie-rock band behind the hit "Feel It Still".',"Arlo Parks with Baird":"British singer-songwriter Arlo Parks, known for soft indie and poetic lyrics, with Baird supporting.",Tinlicker:"Dutch electronic duo, known for melodic house and live-style sets.","Prague Sounds: Max Cooper":"A show by the electronic composer Max Cooper, part of Prague Sounds.",Stahlzeit:"Industrial music night with the band Stahlzeit, who play Rammstein-style material.",Artemas:'British pop singer, known for the 2024 hit "i like the way you kiss me".',"Arab Strap":"Scottish indie duo Arab Strap, known for spoken-word storytelling over moody music.","Prague Sounds: Anoushka Shankar":"Sitar player and composer Anoushka Shankar, part of Prague Sounds.","Papa Roach":'American hard-rock band known for "Last Resort".',"Bach: Violin Sonatas":"Violin sonatas by J. S. Bach, performed in a church setting.","Gerald Clayton":"The American jazz pianist Gerald Clayton live at the Jazz Dock club.","The Witcher III in Concert":"The music from the video game The Witcher 3, performed live by an orchestra.","Alena Hron and Alban Gerhardt":"A classical recital in the Smetana Hall of the Municipal House, with 